 "description": "Why are all flights grounded today? The FAA ground stop explained, as of Fri Nov 13, 2026, 7 pm ET. The FAA ordered a nationwide ground stop on departures from all U.S. airports on Friday afternoon, citing \"extraordinary circumstances and for reasons of safety.\" The Transportation Secretary said a communication issue hit all the Air Route Traffic Control Centers. Planes already in the air kept flying; some were diverted to other airports. As of 7 pm ET, departures were held until further notice, and the FAA said they would resume as systems recover. CBS News, citing sources, reports that a network update made the system reboot and crash; that is not confirmed. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin says there is no indication yet of a nefarious act. This is a developing story: check your airline and the FAA for the latest. The jokes are ours; the facts are sourced below.\n\n#flightsgrounded #faa #groundstop #meatballmyths #shorts\n\nSources: FAA and U.S. Department of Transportation statements (Nov 13, 2026); NBC News, CBS News, ABC News, CNBC and Scripps News coverage (Nov 13, 2026).",
